# GLib's g_strerror() keeps the messages it has converted to UTF-8 in a
# cache for the life of the process.  Valgrind on FreeBSD does not see a
# pointer to one of them and calls it lost; the tests reach it through the
# error path of g_file_get_contents() on a file that is not there.
{
   glib-g_strerror-cache
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:g_strerror
}
